From: TB-X606V kernel project
Subject: [PATCH] ram_console: clear ram_console_buffer_pa when the SRAM mapping fails

The bootloader of the shipping 4.9.190 firmware passes a ram_console DT node this 4.9.117 driver misparses
(0xac000000001@0x8000010dc00), ioremap fails, and the garbage _pa pointer makes every aee_rr_rec_*_pa()
caller oops on a NULL ram_console_buffer. Forcing the Kconfig window instead makes the early boot hang.

---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c b/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/ram_console/mtk_ram_console.c
@@ -681,6 +681,13 @@
 		if (bufp)
 			buffer_size = sram.size;
 		else {
+			/*
+			 * The aee_rr_rec_*_pa() helpers test ram_console_buffer_pa but then dereference
+			 * ram_console_buffer (the failed mapping): keep both NULL or fiq_cache_init and
+			 * mtk_cpuidle_init oops at boot. (Making the mapping succeed instead hangs the
+			 * tablet in the first fraction of a second.)
+			 */
+			ram_console_buffer_pa = NULL;
 			pr_err("ram_console: ioremap failed, [0x%lx, 0x%lx]\n",
 					sram.start,
 			       sram.size);
